# oracle: pair dpd/ext with its random forces on, two atoms (one interacting pair, so the per-pair draw order is the same as native's)
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): engine vs native max relative error 3.0e-15 (thermo), 2.0e-16 (per-atom). Random forces ON (T=1): four deviates per pair, one interacting pair, so the draw order agrees. Pair inside the cutoff for the first ~20 steps.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-12 abs=0
units        lj
boundary     p p p
atom_style   atomic
dimension    3
newton       on
comm_modify  vel yes
region       simBox block 0 5 0 5 0 5
create_box   2 simBox
create_atoms 1 single 1.0 1.0 1.0
create_atoms 2 single 1.5 1.2 1.1
mass         * 1.0
pair_style   dpd/ext 1.0 1.0 3854262
pair_coeff   * * 25.0 4.5 4.53 0.5 0.53 1.0
timestep     0.01
run_style    verlet
velocity all create 1.0 68768932
thermo_style custom step time temp press pe ke
thermo_modify format float %.15g
thermo       10
fix 1 all    nve
run          50
